---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Icon from "../components/Icon.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Verification & estimation methodology"
  description="How Vetlas verifies providers, generates review themes and AI summaries, and computes expense estimates — with explicit minimum-sample gates."
  canonical="/methodology/"
>
  <div class="container">
    <header class="page-head">
      <h1>Methodology</h1>
      <p>
        How data gets onto Vetlas, how it is labelled, and when we allow ourselves to show
        estimates and summaries.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="doc mt-25 pb-1">
      <div class="doc-block">
        <h2><Icon name="badge" class="icon icon-lg" /> Verification logic</h2>
        <p>
          Every profile starts <strong>unverified</strong>. Verified badges appear only after a
          Vetlas team member has checked the evidence by hand, and show the exact date checked.
          Council registration numbers are never verified or displayed — credentials are listed
          exactly as stated, with the source.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="doc-block">
        <h2><Icon name="sparkle" class="icon icon-lg" /> Review themes & AI summaries</h2>
        <p>
          Reputation is built from <strong>recurring themes</strong> extracted across stored
          reviews — each theme shows how many reviews support it. AI-written summaries are
          generated <strong>strictly from stored review IDs</strong> (no hallucinated content) and
          only when <strong>at least 5 public reviews</strong> exist. Summaries are labelled:
          <em>"AI-summarised from N public reviews, updated on &lt;date&gt;"</em>.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="doc-block">
        <h2><Icon name="wallet" class="icon icon-lg" /> Expense estimates</h2>
        <p>
          Consultation fees are kept separate from additional medicine/treatment expenses. Vetlas
          collects user reports of total additional visit cost into tiers — ₹500–1,000,
          ₹1,000–2,500, ₹2,500–5,000 and ₹5,000+. A per-facility estimate is displayed
          <strong>only after at least 10 approved reports in the last 12 months</strong>; below
          that we show "not enough reports yet".
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="doc-block">
        <h2><Icon name="pin" class="icon icon-lg" /> City publication gates</h2>
        <p>
          Cities are published only when profiles meet strict quality thresholds: Tier 1 cities
          need <strong>≥30 vetted profiles</strong> (target 80–100), Tier 2 need
          <strong>≥15</strong> (target 40–50), Tier 3 need <strong>≥5</strong> (target 10–20).
          Cities below the minimum stay unpublished and noindexed.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="doc-block">
        <h2><Icon name="search" class="icon icon-lg" /> Search & indexability</h2>
        <p>
          Combination pages (city × speciality) are indexed only with <strong>≥3 vetted
          providers</strong>; thin profiles are noindexed until they meet quality bars. URL
          structure is lowercase and hyphenated: <code>/{'{'}city{'}'}/</code>,
          <code>/{'{'}city{'}'}/{'{'}speciality{'}'}/</code>,
          <code>/{'{'}city{'}'}/{'{'}provider{'}'}/</code>.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="doc-block">
        <h2><Icon name="info" class="icon icon-lg" /> Zero dark patterns</h2>
        <p>
          No popups, no lead-capture walls, no sponsored listing cards, no fake urgency. If a
          number or claim isn't backed by data, we'd rather say <strong>"not available yet"</strong>
          than invent it.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
